mergeStylesNoList -- mergeStyles (incant/utilities) walks every member of a form, and for each one runs
`for grup in argument; attributes`. firstLight's bar holds a member `space` with no attribute and no member, so it
has no list. A for over a field with no list does one of two things, depending on how its source arrived:
  - it prints "nextGroup: ERROR space does not contain a list" (twice), or
  - it silently walks a holder further up the chain in its place (aCTionFOR, ruleActions.rtn: "if !LoopOn.groupList
    && result  LoopOn = result").
Which one happens depends on what ran just before. Measured 2026-11-27 on trunk: `show(firstLight);` alone is
silent; `include(utilities); show(firstLight);` prints the two lines; a cerr added at mergeStyles' head makes both
print them. With kantGrammar loaded by utilities (branch kantgrammar-once) every show(firstLight) prints them.
Found by lldb: the two lines come from aCTionFOR under mergeStyles under mergeStyles, LoopOn tagged space, no list.

